# jsvalue.hbp from tools/referee.py; do not edit
# ECMA-262 operations the upstream lines apply, written out in Python (not from the Rust port).
# VALUE: v is a value token; truthy = !!v; le_one = (v <= 1) after ToNumber and binary64 rounding;
#   number_or_zero = Number(v) || 0 (ToNumber rounds to binary64) where it is an integer of magnitude
#   <= 2^53, else 'refused' (the port's domain); string = String(v), escaped. GREATER: a > b for two
#   strings or two numbers, else 'refused'. QUOTE: JSON.stringify of a string. NUMTEXT: String(x) of
#   the binary64 with these bits. FROMTEXT: a decimal laid out as String(x) lays out; canonical = 1
#   when it is String(x) of the binary64 value x it rounds to.
# Value tokens: u n t f #<String(x)> '<escaped string> [ ... ] { '<key> <value> ... }, separated by
#   spaces; escapes are %XX for % space | = and bytes below 0x20 and 0x7F.
